    "narrative": "With the 2026 season reaching its final stretch, the Austin Waves offense hinges today on the tandem of **Gunnar Henderson** and **Coby Mayo** against Yesavage. **Gunnar Henderson** stands as our highest-rated play at 83.29, benefiting from a favorable 4.57 xERA matchup and a prime spot in the three-hole. His ability to anchor our stolen base output remains the primary catalyst for his elite valuation. **Coby Mayo** enters with a solid 62.86 score; while the right-on-right dynamic against Yesavage caps his ceiling slightly, the hitter-friendly park factors and his elevated position in the batting order keep him firmly in the \"Strong\" start category.\n\nOur bench decision-making process was relatively straightforward today, largely due to health constraints. While **Kyle Tucker**, **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.**, **Luis Robert Jr.**, and **Andy Pages** occupy the top of our bench rankings, they are unavailable due to team off-days or injury status, leaving no viable candidates to challenge the current lineup. With **Jackson Merrill**, **Jordan Westburg**, **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.**, **Jacob Wilson**, **Drake Baldwin**, **Nasim Nunez**, **Heliot Ramos**, **Josh Jung**, **Miguel Vargas**, **Brayan Rocchio**, **Henry Bolte**, **Tommy White**, **Curtis Mead**, **Sam Antonacci**, **Franklin Arias**, **Dominic Smith**, **Wade Meckler**, **Liam Hicks**, and **Luis Lara** also sidelined, we are banking on the high-floor production of our active duo to navigate a matchup that, while statistically favorable, still requires precision execution to capitalize on the 4.57 xERA of the opposition. No major weather risks are currently flagging in the forecast, so we expect the full allotment of plate appearances for both **Gunnar Henderson** and **Coby Mayo**.",
